42
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:24,000
150 pairs of male lovers. The logic was that lovers would fight fiercely beside one another and feel ashamed to appear

43
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:33,000
cowardly in front of the person whose opinion mattered most. Whether every detail of the later tradition is exact, the idea itself made sense to Greek

44
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:41,000
writers. They did not assume love between men weakened soldiers. They imagined it could make them terrifying.

45
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:49,000
But Greece was not one civilization with one sexual policy. Athens, Sparta, thieves, Cree, and other communities

46
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:58,000
